  "_notes": {
    "taxonomy_source": "Categories mirror the Pitts Ads dataset (Hussain et al., CVPR 2017) and the AdsQA benchmark (arXiv 2509.08621). We use four categories — kept deliberately small so the experiment has at least 3 ads per category and the factor 'ad category' is analytically tractable.",
    "url_status": "All video_url values are either verified public-domain clips from the Internet Archive / Google sample bucket, or locally generated synthetic MP4s (source=synthetic). Synthetic files live in static/ads/ and are generated by scripts/generate_ads.py (requires Pillow + ffmpeg).",
    "how_to_use_in_ads_slots": "Each entry in experiment.json's ads array can either inline the legacy fields (url, placement, etc.) or set library_ref to one of the ids below; the player resolves library_ref before scheduling. See app.py::resolve_ad().",
    "synthetic_ad_pairs": "ad_relevant_screentime / ad_relevant_arcademax are thematically relevant to entertainment content. ad_irrelevant_crunchpop / ad_irrelevant_homesafe are clearly unrelated. Use these to pilot-test relevance effects or to assign matched vs mismatched ads to conditions."
  },
